# TASK008 BCG-CORONA - ordinal regression: ongoing conditions (MHONGO) vs COVID-19 severity

## Headline (pre-specified primary model)
**+63.8% odds of higher COVID-19 severity per additional ongoing medical condition**
(OR 1.6378, 95% CI [1.464, 1.832] = [46.4%, 83.2%]; beta 0.4934 , SE 0.0572; p = 6.6e-18; n = 1000).
Estimator: proportional-odds (cumulative logit) ordinal regression, statsmodels OrderedModel.
Outcome = max AEHS over clinical AEs (AECAT RTI/Other, ISR excluded), 6 collapsed levels (0,1,2,3,4,5+); patients with no clinical AE = 0.
Predictor = count of MHONGO='Yes' records per USUBJID. Adjusted: TRTGRP (BCG vs Placebo), patients_seen, work_hours, expect_interact.
Raw 0-7 outcome gives 63.7% (shift 0.1 pp).

